  "id": "reinforcer",
  "term": "reinforcer",
  "definition": "A reinforcer is something that makes a behavior happen more often because it is presented after that behavior. Common examples include rewards such as food, water, or opportunities to explore, and some drugs can also act as reinforcers.",
